      "widgets_values": [
        "subject_definitions:\n<Picture 1> is the facial identity and hairstyle reference for the adult man. <Picture 2> is this SAME person's exact wardrobe and footwear reference. Preserve this person's identity; do not take the studio setting or pose from the references. This is <Subject 1>.\n\nsummary:\nA frame from an understated contemporary Japanese romantic feature film. Real live-action photographic cinematography, naturally imperfect skin and fabric, soft optical halation, subtle fine 35mm grain, restrained exposure and color, no HDR or over-sharpening. Thoughtful off-center composition with foreground depth and negative space. Quiet observational camera, plausible physical space, no beauty advertising, no studio or character sheet, no collage, no illustration, no CGI. No text, letters, subtitles, signage, watermarks, logos, or black bars. Keep the supplied adult identities and exact wardrobes while replacing the studio setting completely.\nA remembered afternoon in the same Japanese coastal town. Soft late-afternoon sunlight, pale blue-green sea, faded olive details, honey-colored wood, warm cream skin, delicate golden backlight. Warm but realistic, not orange-tinted or sepia.\n\ndetailed_description:\n[Shot 1] Intimate close-up of the man in beige linen suit, face angled slightly right toward his offscreen companion. Same harbor afternoon, sea and old pale buildings blurred behind. Natural relaxed smile, 85mm lens, soft side light. This is a single still opening frame of one continuous movie shot. Keep the scene specific and lived-in. Use all identity and wardrobe references only for their assigned people. A coherent photographic composition, no panel layout, no split screen.\n",
